        "eyebrow": "Common questions",
        "heading": "Permanent lighting, answered straight"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does permanent lighting cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Permanent architectural lighting runs $27 per linear foot of roofline. A typical home with 150 to 250 feet of roofline lands between $4,000 and $6,750. Add-ons are flat rate: Smart App Control is $500 and a Power box is $500, required on any roofline over 200 feet. You can price your own home on our <a href=\"/pages/estimate\">estimate page</a> — real rates, no sales call.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will the lights survive a hard winter?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The track and diodes are rated for real winters — freeze-thaw cycles, snow load on the eave and full summer sun on a south-facing roofline. Craftsmanship and lighting are both backed by a 10-year warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the install take?",
            "answer": "<p>Most single-family homes are finished in one day. Larger or multi-gable rooflines can run into a second day. We confirm the timeline before we start and the crew cleans the site before leaving.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I change the colors myself?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. With Smart App Control you run color, brightness, scenes and schedules from your phone — no ladder, no swapping bulbs. Holiday, game day and accent scenes are built in and ready with one tap.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the hardware visible during the day?",
            "answer": "<p>The channel is mounted flush to the roofline and color-matched, so from the street it reads as trim. That is the point of a custom install rather than a clip-on strip.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are you licensed and insured?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — Kilowash is licensed and insured, and every install is done by our own crew. See <a href=\"/pages/testimonials\">reviews and finished projects</a> for recent work.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
